<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Adaptive launcher foreground (108x108 viewport).

  Artwork is the traced bud pair from drawable/ic_bud_left.xml and
  drawable/ic_bud_right.xml — the same vectors the widget uses — arranged
  side by side as if sitting in the case.

  Both buds are placed with <group> transforms, so the original traced path
  data is reused verbatim rather than redrawn.

  GEOMETRY (derived, not eyeballed - see the numbers below)

  Ink bounds of each source path, in the 48x48 source space:
      left  : x 8.6 -> 38.1  (centre 23.35), y 0.3 -> 47.5 (centre 23.90)
      right : x 9.5 -> 39.2  (centre 24.35), y 0.3 -> 47.5 (centre 23.90)

  The right bud is mirrored (scaleX = -S) so the two face each other. Under
  x' = Tx + (-S)*x the mirrored ink centre lands at Tx - S*cx. For the pair to
  be centred horizontally on the viewport centre C (=54) with an ink gap of G
  between the two inner edges, both bud centres must sit at C +/- (S*w + G)/2.

  Chosen: G = 5.0 units (gap between inner edges), S = 0.756.
      w = 29.5 (mean ink width), so half-step = (0.756*29.5 + 5.0)/2 = 13.65
      left  ink centre x = 54 - 13.65 = 40.35  -> Tx = 40.35 - 0.756*23.35 = 22.14
      right ink centre x = 54 + 13.65 = 67.65  -> Tx = 67.65 + 0.756*24.35 = 86.62

  Vertically, ink centre 23.90 must map to C = 54:
      Ty = 54 - 0.756*23.90 = 35.93

  Resulting ink box: x 28.64 -> 79.44, y 36.16 -> 71.84. Centred on 54 in both
  axes.

  WHY S = 0.756 AND NOT SOMETHING BIGGER: the safe zone is a CIRCLE of radius 33
  (not a 66-unit square), so the binding test is the distance of each ink CORNER
  from the centre, not each axis independently. At S=0.62 the worst corner sat
  at radius 25.58, i.e. the artwork filled only 77.5% of the safe circle and read
  as undersized next to other launcher icons. The pair is wide and short, so its
  width is what limits growth.

  At S=0.756 the worst corner is at radius 31.04, which is 94.1% of the safe
  radius: visibly larger while keeping a margin against antialiasing and mask
  variance. Do NOT raise this toward 33/25.58 = 1.29 (the exact-touch limit) -
  there would be no margin left.

  If the artwork is retraced, RE-SOLVE: max over the four ink corners of the
  distance from (54,54), then pick a scale whose worst corner lands near 31.

  Monochrome by design: solid white on the black ic_launcher_background. No
  accent colour, no dots.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">

    <!-- Left bud: source 48x48 scaled 0.756; ink centre -> x 40.35, y 54. -->
    <group
        android:scaleX="0.756"
        android:scaleY="0.756"
        android:translateX="22.14"
        android:translateY="35.93">
        <path
            android:fillColor="#FFFFFF"
            android:pathData="M 25.8 47.5 L 22.7 47.2 L 21.4 46.4 L 20.0 44.9 L 19.3 43.0 L 19.1 39.7 L 19.1 27.3 L 16.6 27.2 L 14.6 26.7 L 12.4 25.4 L 10.4 23.4 L 9.1 21.2 L 8.6 19.4 L 8.6 16.1 L 9.1 14.2 L 10.8 11.4 L 13.8 9.0 L 15.8 5.5 L 18.5 3.0 L 22.9 0.8 L 25.3 0.3 L 29.0 0.3 L 32.7 1.6 L 36.5 5.2 L 37.9 8.5 L 38.1 12.6 L 37.4 15.1 L 35.5 18.3 L 33.4 20.6 L 30.4 22.9 L 30.6 43.2 L 29.6 45.2 L 28.4 46.4 Z" />
    </group>

    <!--
      Right bud: mirrored to face the left one, as they sit in the case.
      scaleX = -0.756 puts ink at x = 86.62 - 0.756*x (centre 67.65).
    -->
    <group
        android:scaleX="-0.756"
        android:scaleY="0.756"
        android:translateX="86.62"
        android:translateY="35.93">
        <path
            android:fillColor="#FFFFFF"
            android:pathData="M 23.8 47.5 L 21.0 47.4 L 19.6 46.6 L 18.6 45.8 L 17.4 43.9 L 17.1 42.8 L 17.3 22.7 L 15.0 21.1 L 11.9 17.9 L 10.1 14.4 L 9.5 11.8 L 9.9 8.1 L 12.1 4.1 L 14.8 1.8 L 18.8 0.3 L 24.2 0.6 L 27.1 1.8 L 29.7 3.4 L 32.8 6.6 L 34.1 9.2 L 35.3 9.9 L 37.8 12.6 L 39.2 16.6 L 39.0 19.9 L 37.0 23.8 L 33.6 26.5 L 31.2 27.2 L 28.7 27.3 L 28.3 43.4 L 27.6 45.0 L 26.0 46.6 Z" />
    </group>
</vector>
